// REJECTS: NullPointerException
//
// `actions:` on a HostedService. An island type whose processor does not exist: nothing in
// legend-engine implements IPostDeploymentActionGrammarParserExtension -- zero implementors
// repo-wide -- so HostedServiceTreeWalker:150 throws for every action type a user could
// name.
//
// But it does not reach that throw. The bare form CRASHES first: the grammar makes
// actionBody optional (`postDeploymentAction: actionType (actionBody)?`) and the walker
// dereferences spec.actionBody().actionValue() unconditionally. This is the SECOND
// NullPointerException of exactly this shape -- see ./walker-rejected-projects.pure and F17
// -- an optional grammar element dereferenced without a null check, surfacing as a stack
// trace with no source information.
//
// The braced form `actions: [ MyAction { actionValue: 'x'; } ]` does not help: the runner's
// 4.138.2 grammar rejects it at the brace with "Valid alternatives: [',', ']']". So no
// spelling of this keyword reaches a working parser.
###HostedService
HostedService fixture::neg::CrashingAction
{
   pattern: '/hs';
   ownership: Deployment { identifier: '1' };
   function: fixture::neg::f():String[1];
   actions: [ MyAction ];
}
